---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/it/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"deliver\", \"--help\"])"
---
Hand a file or folder to a daemon this device paired with, which receives it into its inbox

Usage: sluice deliver [OPTIONS] <DEVICE> <PATH>

Arguments:
  <DEVICE>
          The paired daemon's name, or a prefix of its endpoint id

  <PATH>
          The file or folder to deliver

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --name <NAME>
          The top-level name the content takes under the daemon's inbox. Without it the delivery is named by the ticket's root in hex

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
